 he other half of the story of conflict: what it takes for individuals\, co
 mmunities and nations to rebuild and heal after war. One photographer rece
 ives a USD 25\,000 grant to produce a post-conflict body of work\, and fou
 r finalists are named\; winners are announced by the end of December 2026.
 \n\nOrganisation: The Aftermath Project\nLocation: Worldwide. Open to work
 ing photographers anywhere\, for projects about the aftermath of conflict.
 \nAward: One USD 25\,000 production grant (paid 50% at start\, 40% midway\
 , 10% on delivery)\; four additional finalists named. No application fee s
 tated.\nDuration: Grant work must be completed by 1 January 2028\; photogr
 aphs delivered by 1 May 2028.\n\nMore: https://www.theaftermathproject.org
 /application/2026-post-conflict-grant-application?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
